# 🧬 Permission Alchemy — A Permit.io x Glyph Tier Integration Demo

This is a symbolic access control demo using **Permit.io's declarative permission logic** fused with our **3-tier glyph authorization system** from the Nibiru project.

## 🔮 Tier Mapping

| Permit Layer       | Mapped Glyph Tier         | Description                          |
|--------------------|---------------------------|--------------------------------------|
| `user.attributes`  | Tier 1 – Identity Tier     | Who they are                         |
| `resource`         | Tier 2 – Object Tier       | What they’re accessing               |
| `action`           | Tier 3 – Behavior Tier     | How and how often they’re interacting |

This forms the basis of what we call **Permission Alchemy** — symbolic access enforcement at scale.

## 🛠 Files & Features

- `glyph.tsx`: Simulates glyph interaction with access control
- `GlyphAccess.tsx`: Visual component for permission feedback
- `permitCheck.ts`: Mocked Permit.io logic for local testing
- `login.tsx`: Placeholder login to choose a test user tier

## 🧪 Test Accounts

| Username          | Tier | Outcome           |
|-------------------|------|-------------------|
| `user-123`        | 3    | ✅ Access Granted |
| `user-guardian`   | 2    | ❌ Denied         |
| `user-initiate`   | 1    | ❌ Denied         |

## 🧩 Expandable Concepts

- Visual permission threads (glyph-node overlay)
- AI denial reasoning: “Insufficient Resonance”
- Role templates: Artist, Guardian, Initiate
- Pod/AI-based cross-permission layers

## 🚀 Integration Ready

This is a public-safe fragment of a larger system running inside the [Nibiru AI infrastructure](https://nibiru.site). All logic can be upgraded to call live `permit.check()` endpoints via Permit.io CLI or SDK.

